<p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/02BH">Example <span data-tag="02BH">2.4.6.5</span>.</a> Let $\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}$ be a strict bicategory (Definition <a data-tag="007L" href="/tag/007L">2.2.0.1</a>) and let $\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}_{\bullet }$ denote the associated simplicial category (Example <a data-tag="00KA" href="/tag/00KA">2.4.2.8</a>). Then the homotopy category $\operatorname {h}\! \mathit{\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}_{\bullet }}$ of the simplicial category $\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}_{\bullet }$ (in the sense of Construction <a data-tag="00LX" href="/tag/00LX">2.4.6.1</a>) can be identified with the coarse homotopy category $\operatorname {h}\! \mathit{\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}}$ of $\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}$ (in the sense of Construction <a data-tag="02AS" href="/tag/02AS">2.2.8.2</a>). </p>
